SMOOTH MACH DYNAMICS Examples

aluminum_strip_pull : a 2d strip of aluminum is elongated until failure
fluid_structure_interaction : multiple solid objects interact with fluid flow, 2d
funnel_flow: fluid flows through a complex 3d object read from a .STL file
rubber_rings_3d: two solid bodies impact each other and deform
rubber_strip_pull: a 2d check for the correctness of linear elasticity

Most of these inputs run only a small number of time steps by default,
so that they can also be used for regression testing.  For those, the
number of time steps is set with the index style variable "nsteps",
which can be changed from the command line with the -var flag:

aluminum_strip_pull : default 2000, use "-var nsteps 30000" to reach failure
fluid_structure_interaction : default 4000, use "-var nsteps 10000" for the full example
funnel_flow : default 2000, use "-var nsteps 5000" for the full example
rubber_rings_3d : default 2000, use "-var nsteps 5000" for the full example

Example: lmp -in in.aluminum_strip_pull -var nsteps 30000

See the MACHDYN how to page in the LAMMPS documentation,
https://docs.lammps.org/Howto_machdyn.html
for a detailed explanation of these examples.
